      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَدَأَهُ</span></b> , aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَدَأُ</span>, <i>He made it even</i> or <i>plain.</i>
(K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See 5. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ودأ</span> (aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَدَأُ</span>, T) <i>Veretrum
exseruit</i> equus: (T, K:) but AHeyth says that
this is an error, and that the correct word is
without <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ء</span>: [i. e., <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَدَى</span>, q.v.]. (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَأْنِى</span>
[imp.], <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَعْنِى</span>, <i>Let me</i> &amp;c. (K.) Said by
some to be of weak authority. (TA.)

